Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 47 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast cancer  Short stitch equals superior  long stitch equals lateral                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  LEFT  AXILLARY SENTINEL   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE LYMPH NODE  SEE NOTE   Note  The metastatic deposit is greater than 0 2cm and extracapsular extension is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 56                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm gray to tan pink firm lymph node with minimal attached tan yellow adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted as A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating superior margin and a long stitch the lateral margin  The specimen is partially surface by a REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm gray tan unremarkable skin ellipse  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two poorly demarcated areas of hemorrhage and associated tan yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The former focally abuts the posterior margin  and the latter focally abuts the anterior margin  No discrete mass lesion is grossly appreciated  and there is an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm area of dense gray white fibrotic tissue which focally abuts the inferoposterior margin  Sections of the two hemorrhagic areas and gray white fibrous tissue in B G are submitted as B G  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JULIE ANN NAGLE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   Tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Add