nk grossly unremarkable skin ellipse which in turns bears a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm grossly unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The anterior surface is inked but and the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm hemorrhagic cavitary lesion in the lower inner quadrant  approximately 4 o clock   with vaguely fibrotic surrounding parenchyma  This lesion extends to 2 4cm to the closest posterior margin  and approximately 1 1cm to the closest anterior margin  Sectioning reveals multifocally fibrous tissue with no additional discrete lesions identified  No lymph nodes are identified  A clip is identified within the body of the aforementioned cavity lesion  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest black inked posterior margins to cavitary lesion  Note  No gross lesion in these sections    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitary lesion  entirely  from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   RIGHT BREAST SENTINEL NODE   NO CARCINOMA SEEN  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Saturday REMOVED_MONTH 03   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 34 00PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla   Sentinel    Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART C  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only   report_end  , Unchecked.
