ections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm with an axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is attached to an ellipse of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm which includes the nipple  The nipple displays a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white nodule 4 5cm lateral to the nipple there is a puckered indentation  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a poorly circumscribed fibrous lesion that appears to extend to the deep margin of resection in a region designated by the surgeon with a stitch  This area corresponds to the puckered lesion on the skin s surface  An accurate measurement of this area cannot be given due to poor circumscription and diffuse fibrosis surrounding the lesion  Dissection of the axillary tail reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to up to 0 9cm in largest dimension  Section code  A F  Lymph nodes  G  Lesion to deep margin  H I  Lesion including skin  puckered area  and deep margin J K L  Additional sections of fibrous region M  Nipple with white nodule  T X  Additional sections  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a simple mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  The overlying ellipse of skin  including the nipple  is unremarkable and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal diffusely fibrotic breast parenchyma  One focal lesion is identified in the subareola region consisting of a poorly defined firm area within the fibrotic breast parenchyma spanning approximately 1 5cm in largest dimension  This area is located approximately 0 8cm from the deep margin of resection  Sections are taken as follows  Section code  N O  Suspicious focus  entirely submitted  cassette N  lesion to deep margin   P S  Representative sections of fibrotic breast parenchyma  Y CC  Additional sections Resident  ADRIANO PIRIS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
