s prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is an unoriented simple mastectomy specimen measuring 21 x 14 x 4 5cm  There is an overlying wrinkled  tan skin ellipse which has a 1 0cm retracted nipple  At one end of the skin ellipse  there is a 3 8cm well healed surgical incision  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink purple papule that approaches one skin margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm biopsy cavity which is fibrotic and hemorrhagic  The surrounding tissue shows fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located 1 5cm from the deep margin  No residual tumor is grossly appreciated  Further sectioning of the breast reveals yellow fatty tissue with a moderate amount of gray white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  gray white nodule located 3 5cm from the skin margin  6 5cm from the biopsy cavity and grossly a