Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 21 CLINICAL DATA  DCIS at surgical margin  previous excision  Sutures  Long   lateral  short   superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA   SLIDE D   REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE HEALING BIOPSY SITES  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITES  3   5  INTRAMAMMARY LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite angiolymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of resection appear free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain sufficient numbers of invasive tumor cells to permit interpretation  See note  Note  Rare in situ high grade tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein and rare in situ high grade tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 AUG 98 at 14 09 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm  The skin has an 8 0cm scar down the midline  The lateral aspect is demarcated by a long stitch  the superior is demarcated by a short stitch  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm stellate  fibrous area with focal areas of hemorrhage  The fibrous area extends to within 0 8cm of the posterior inked margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white nodule  which is approximately 0 2cm from the posterior margin and 5 0cm from the lateral margin  Approximately 14 0cm from the medial margin  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  centrally located  hemorrhagic nodule with surrounding areas of fatty necrosis  This nodule comes to within 3 0cm of the posterior margin  10 0cm from the medial margin  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic nodule with areas of fatty necrosis  which is approximately 2 0cm from the posterior deep margin  The cut surface of the medial and lateral breast parenchyma are grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A D  Biopsy cavity with deep margin  E   Skin  F   Lateral  small nodule  G I  Centrally located hemorrhagic nodule  J K  Most medial hemorrhagic nodule  L   Medial margin  M   Lateral margin  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD   