97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  lumpectomy  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of breast with a short stitch indicating the superior margin  a long stitch indicating the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  deep margin  black  inferior margin  blue  superior margin  red  and the anterior margin  green  A section is made at the inferior margin to reveal an irregularly defined  firm  white mass measuring 1 2cm in greatest dimension and coming to within 0 1cm from the inferior margin  The specimen is submitted in its entirety from the lateral to medial margin in cassettes A through H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  additional margin inferior cavity  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibrofatty yellow tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a grossly unremarkable yellow fatty parenchyma  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes I through M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node contents  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue from which multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in length from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in length are dissected away  The nodes are submitted in cassettes M through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional node content  left axilla  is a 1 x 1 x 0 3cm piece of yellow fatty tissue  Dissected away from the tissue is one tan pink lymph node measuring 1cm in length  The lymph node is bisected and one half is submitted in cassette Q  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  APPROACHING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INFERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  ERIN OCHOA  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Robert Joseph Carey Jr   M D  PART A  LUMPECTOMY  BREAST  LEFT  PART B  BREAST  ADDITIONAL  LEFT  PART C  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS PART D  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
