ck  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    EXCISION  METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  SEE TABLE  2   LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  SEE TABLE  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  BOTH SPECIMENS  TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2 TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  12 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2  including a 1 9cm node replaced by tumor  Extracapsular extension  Present  slight  Other forms of axillary involvement  None By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast biopsy   is a portion of fibrofatty tissue  with an inserted needle localization wire  with one suture designating medial and two sutures designating superior  There is an accompanying radiograph  The specimen measures 8 0cm from medial to lateral  6 0cm from superior to inferior and 1 7cm from anterior to posterior  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm tan skin ellipse on the anterior   lateral aspect of the specimen  displaying diffuse blue dye  consistent with sentinel node dye  The specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  and inferior yellow and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm irregular ill defined white tan firm mass  This mass is 0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  1 0cm from the inferior margin  2 5cm from the superior margin  1 8cm from the medial margin and 1 2cm from the lateral margin  There is also a REMOVE