 OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The intraductal proliferations display a spectrum of cytologic and architectural changes  Focally  there are cribriform spaces and mucin production as seen in the DCIS of the previous excision  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    consistent with residual ductal carcinoma in situ  Cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE stain is focally negative in this area  which supports the diagnosis  Multiple levels were examined   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Ducts lined by atypical glandular cells and containing luminal mucin are negative for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE and interpreted as foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia  In other areas  the ductal proliferations are more likely to represent ductal epithelial hyperplasia of the usual type  which is also supported by positive cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE staining   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Dr  F  Koerner has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis and interpretation  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross description  BREAST  LEFT SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE OR IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  see individual gross description  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fatty tissue within which a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm lymph node is identified  The lymph node is bisected and submitted in its entirety for frozen as FX 1 and 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  respectively  Received in formali