ION  Received are 4 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is dissected and palpated to reveal a single candidate lymph node  up to 1 2cm in greatest dimension  which is bisected and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen  received with a suture designating the axillary aspect  as per the surgeon  The anterior aspect is partially surfaced by a 2 0cm in diameter unremarkable wrinkled areola  bearing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unremarkable  everted nipple  The specimen is inked for orientation as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Sectioning reveals predominantly gray white  dense  rubbery fibrous tissue occupying approximately 60  of the cut surfaces  There are focally gritty  irregular areas within the upper inner and upper outer quadrants  No masses are grossly identified  Also in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan strip of hair bearing unremarkable skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative separately received skin strip  Received fresh  labeled  right breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm unoriented mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of tan  wrinkled  hair bearing skin with a 2 5cm in length  well healed  C shaped scar  The unremarkable brown  wrinkled areola measures 2 4cm in dia