 with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 54 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of oriented fibroadipose tissue  A short stitch designates the superior margin and a long stitch the lateral  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm ill defined  tan  firm stellate mass extending within 0 1cm from the inferior margin  0 6cm from the lateral margin  0 7cm from the medial margin  and 0 5cm from the superior margin  No frozen section is performed  Section Code  A D  the mass in its entirety  cassette A and D has mass with closest  inferior  margin  E  superior margin  F  medial margin  G  lateral margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary lymphadenectomy Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm irregular portion of adipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging from 0 2cm in greatest dimension to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  A representative section of each is submitted in cassettes H   K  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary lymphadenectomy Level 