Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 34 CLINICAL DATA  Hypoechoic mass 2 o clock left breast r o malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  2 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES  FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE SEE ADDENDUM  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin light chains there is no staining of tumor cells  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a follicular pattern  The B cells are positive for antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The tumor cells are also positive for bcl 2 and focally for Ki 67  approximately 10    The tumor cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15 20 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 2 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A  Gross Description by  JIM BRADLEY Resident  WEN JING  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Elizabeth A Rafferty  M D  Charles Harris Weiss  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  2 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  56 year old female with left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   ADENOCARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  INVASIVE GRADE III III  FOCALLY MUCIN SECRETORY  REMOVED_DATE CM IN MAXIMUM DIMENSION  NOTE  Several foci of tumor in lymphatic spaces are identified  Tumor is present in 1 of 6 lymph nodes  Representative sections from the margins are free of tumor  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  04 MAY 95 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified breast radical mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm axillary tail  On the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a 0 9cm in diameter nipple and a 2 5cm in diameter areolar complex  2 5cm from the superior skin margin  on the skin ellipse is a 0 6cm suture  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  On cross section  there is an area of firm  white tissue that is directly underneath the skin suture previously noted  This area of white  firm tissue measures a 5 0cm in width and 5 0cm in superior inferior dimension  It comes to within 1 5cm of the closest deep margin  2 5cm from the closest inferior margin  and 5 0cm from the superior margin  In this area of white  firm tissue there are areas of focal hemorrhage  There is no biopsy cavity present  SECTION CODE  A  tumor with closest deep inked margin  B D  tumor with deep inked margin  E  most lateral extension of the tumor  F  area of white  fibrous bands  medial and discontinuous with the medial extent of the tumor  G  representative section from the biopsy site  H  representative section through the nipple with underlying breast  I  skin with suture and underlying breast  J L  additional dissected lymph nodes  M  representative section from the medial margin  N  representative section from the superior margin  O  representative section from the inferior margin  P  representative section from the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse  Resident  M  Prisci