Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA  Mammogram  left breast  shows calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA 80   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU 20   WELL TO MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor focally has a tubular carcinoma pattern  Focal perineural and intraneural extension of tumor is seen  Tumor focally extends to the inked margin of the specimen  A duct distant from the tumor contains severely atypical epithelial cells  possibly representing pagetoid spread of tumor  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 08                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cell stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 20     FLOW CYTOMETRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lobular piece of yellow tissue with a needle localization wire  The external surface is inked  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  stellate  white to tan lesion measuring 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The lesion is within 0 1cm of the margin  The portions of the specimen including the nodule are submitted in cassettes A through C  the remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes D through G  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS GROSS  LEFT BREAST BX   NO LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS FOR DIAGNOSIS  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BX   report_end  , Unchecked.
