PTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The invasive tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The invasive tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  There is a mixed population of ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells represented on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   a large component of the ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells is positive for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins  approximately 50    The remainder of DCIS does not stain for hormone receptor proteins  All ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells show strong overexpression  3   of HER 2 c erbB 2  similar to the invasive carcinoma  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  736  to chromosome 17 signals  87  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN INFERIOR   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN DEEP   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN SUPERIOR   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN LATERAL   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MARGIN MEDIAL   EXCISI  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 58 CLINICAL DATA  44 year old female  excision of right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2 5CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED RESECTION MARGINS  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this an