one binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number is a left modified radical mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm attatched axillary tail  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm tan skin ellipse with an eccentric 2 5cm nipple   areolar complex located 1 0cm from the inferior skin margin  There is a 4 5cm curvi linear surgical incision which is closed by three sutures and located 2 0cm supero lateral to the nipple  The skin ellipse has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan purple macule  which abuts the infero medial margin and a 0 3cm red pink macule located 2 6cm medial to the nipple  Sectioning beneath the incision reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm defect packed with gauze  Adjacent to this defect  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm irregular  indurated  gritty  gray white to yellow mass  which is focally hemorrhagic  This mass is located 1 5cm from the deep margin and 1 4cm from the skin surface  Located 2 0cm inferiorly from the mass  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm firm  gray white nodule  The remaining breast parenchyma is predominately fatty tissue with a small amount of gritty  soft  gray white fibrous tissue  No other lesions or masses are grossly appreciated or palpated  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  The cut surfaces of the nodes range from gray white to yellow and fatty  A representative section of each lymph node is submitted  SECTION CODE  A B  Tumor to deep margin  C E  Tumor  F   Skin overlying tumor  G   Both skin lesions  e