Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 09 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS OF INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  5   ARISING IN THE BACKGROUND OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE  95    2  RADIAL SCARS  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  The focus of invasion is less than 0 1cm in greatest dimension and is not present at a margin  The in situ component aggregates to approximately 1cm in cross sectional surface area  In situ carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the closest resection margin  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The intraductal tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The intraductal tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  The sections stained for hormone receptor proteins do not contain infiltrating carcinoma  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm breast biopsy with a needle localization wire in place and an accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm granular  tan pink area with yellow flecks and focal calcification corresponding to the area of microcalcifiation at the needle tip on the accompanying x ray  This lesion abuts the inked resection margin  The lesion is submitted in A through D  with remainder of breast tissue in E through H  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR IN SITU CARCINOMA  FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASION NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 05 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO INKED RESECTION MARGINS  ASSOCIATED WITH EXTENSIVE CALCIUM DEPOSITION  2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma measures 1 5cm from the glass slide  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is noted  Hormone analysis studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm breast segment with an accompanying guide wire and mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 6cm tan white firm area  The remainder of parenchyma is tan yellow and unremarkable  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  with the suspicious areas for carcinoma in A and B  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
