at he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left sentinel node  REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of soft tissue with two lymph nodes  One is inked black  one blue  Both are bivalved and entirely submitted for frozen as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm left oriented simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior  long stitch designating lateral margin  The anterior surface is surfaced by REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm tan brown skin ellipse which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and 0 5cm inverted nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a mass and an indurated nodule  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  lies approximately between 7 00 and 8 o clock position in the inner quadrant  3 5cm from overlying anterior  and 1 0cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma adjacent to this mass is tan white  nodular  and has a gritty feel  Approximately 3 0cm medial to this mass  approximately in the central quadrant there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink  indurated ill defined area which lies 3 5cm from overlying ink and 2 5cm from posterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma between the mass and this indurated area has gritty feel  The breast parenchyma underneath the inverted nipple is grossly unremarkable and is previously inked blue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  The remaining breast parenchyma contains dense fibrous tissue interspersed with tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire mass to closest posterior inked margin  between 7 00 and 8 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire indurated nodule to include closest posterior inked margin  central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous nodular breast parenchyma between the mass and indurated nodule in central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  fibrous breast parenchyma  upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  nodular breast parenchyma  inner upper quadrant  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left nonsentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink intact node with attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue up to 0 5cm  The entire specimen is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT SENTINEL NODE   NO CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORKUP ON PERMANENT SECTION  Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreacti