Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 25 CLINICAL DATA  64 year old white female with previous left breast biopsy REMOVED_DATE with pathology revealing poorly differentiated  Grade III III  invasive ductal carcinoma with positive margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  PARTIAL MASTECTOMY   1  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE   SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT IN ONE OF EIGHT SLIDES ADJACENT TO BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  All examined margins are free of invasive carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  Residual invasive carcinoma is not seen  LYMPH NODES   LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS    ALL  11  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS    ONE LYMPH NODE IS FREE OF CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 38                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left partial mastectomy  is an ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and on its surface has a linear scar running almost the entire length  Attached to the undersurface is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm mass of fibrofatty tissue  With the long suture  lateral margin  oriented at the 12 o clock position and the short suture  superior margin  at the 9 o clock position  the top half  lateral margin  is double inked in green and the bottom half  medial margin  in black only  The tissue is serially sectioned to reveal a cystic cavity which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Surrounding this cavity is an area of firm  white fibrous tissue  At its closest approximation to the inked surface the cavity comes to within 0 3cm of the black inked medial margin  and at the 3 o clock end comes to within 0 1cm of the green inked lateral margin  Section Code  A B  3 o clock end in which the cystic cavity extends closest to the green inked margin  inferolateral margin   C D  from the 3 o clock half of the ellipse with the cystic cavity coming closest to within the black inked margin  medial   E  a section from the mid portion of the ellipse where which there is white firm fibrous tissue and small punctate yellow areas adjacent to the cystic cavity  F  section from the 9 o clock half of the ellipse in which there is abundant white firm fibrous tissue  G  section from the 9 o clock end of the ellipse in which there is a small area of cystic cavity with white fibrous tissue surrounding it  H  portion of the overlying skin ellipse and underlying cystic cavity from the mid portion of the ellipse  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm segment of fibrofatty tissue containing approximately 12 discrete firm nodules which representative sections are submitted in cassettes I through M  Received in a separate container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Additional axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm brown tan lymph node which is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette N  Resident  RAFFAELE PENNELLA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Susan M Ystueta  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   RESECTION PART B  AXILLA  LEFT   DISSECTION PART C  ADDITIONAL AXILLA   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 32 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old woman with right breast mass  Positive fine needle aspiration                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  MUCINOUS  COLLOID  CARCINOMA  1 4 CM   50   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH COMEDO AND SOLID PATTERNS  50    SEE NOTE  NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IS PRESENT IN MANY OF THE SECTIONS  AND EXTENDS TO THE SUPEROLATERAL AND INFEROLATERAL RESECTION MARGINS  COLLOID CARCINOMA IS NOT PRESENT AT ANY MARGIN  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   DISSECTION  TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 30 Consulting Pathologist s   Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast mass  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm  fibrofatty tissue fragment with two stitches  one short  superior  and one long  lateral   Inked and sectioned to reveal a hard  tan white mass centrally  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The mass is 0 6cm  from the nearest margin which is anterior  Radial margin laterally at the long stitch in A  Radial margin superiorly at the short stitch in B  The superior portion of the tissue fragment submitted lateral to medial in C E G J L N  and P  The inferior portion of the fragment submitted from lateral to medial in D F H I K M O  and Q  A representative fragment of tumor is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Hormone receptors taken  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  fragment is given for research  Labeled with patient s unit number  right axilla nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm fibroadipose tissue fragment containing multiple lymph nodes  pink tan  REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in diameter  Lymph nodes in R through W  Resident  William H  Yong  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION  COLLOID CARCINOMA  INKED MARGINS GROSSLY FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOW