lows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One lymph node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Six lymph nodes intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes bisected  one inked black  Received in fixative  labeled  Diomi Orfanos  REMOVED_DATE  left breast lateral final  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a suture at one aspect  The sutured aspect is inked  and the submitted entirely in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION PART F  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast excisional biopsy specimen  with an attached 5 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The entire specimen is inked black  with the deep margin  posterior  overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  It is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a tan gray  1 2cm in largest dimension  firm mass  focally abutting the anterior soft tissue margin  and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Sectioning of the tissue away from the mass reveals a 0 6cm in largest dimension area of tan grittiness  coming to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  in the medial portion of the specimen  There is a third area of grittiness  0 2cm in largest dimension  coming to within 0 6cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the tissue is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A C  Firm nodule with anterior and posterior margins  D  Representative section of nodule  E  Gritty area  F  Second gritty area  G H  Representative sections  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA CLOSE TO ANTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 49 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1 WITH EXTENSIVE MUCIN PRODUCTION  COLLOID CARCINOMA   REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with localization wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm rubbery  tan  slightly translucent  well circumscribed nodule  located less than 0 1cm from the inked resection margin  Representative section of the nodule is frozen as FX  1  resubmitted in cassette A  The entire remaining sections are submitted in cassettes B through I  Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  CONSISTENT WITH COLLOID CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENT FOR FURTHER SAMPLING TO RULE OUT DUCTAL COMPONENT  O R  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD O R  Staff Pathologist  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  100   FORMING MANY TINY NODULES  PRESENT IN ALL THE SECTIONS  AND ABUTTING THE MARGINS AT SEVERAL POINTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The largest nodule measures 0 4cm  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal an unremarkable breast parenchyma  None frozen  Submitted in toto in A through G  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION IS LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
