ics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 3cm breast specimen with a long suture designating the lateral and a short suture designating the superior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  medial red  lateral yellow  posterior black  anterior blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm well circumscribed mass which abuts focally the anterior margin  The mass is more than 0 3cm from all other margins  Representative sections of the tumor in relation to surgical margins are in A D  representative sections of firm areas away from tumor in E H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  final shave margin   is a 8 x 6 x 0 8cm fragment of fatty breast tissue with a black inked surface designating the edge furthest from tumor  A long stitch designates the inferior and short stitch the medial margin  The inferior margin is overinked red and the medial margin overinked yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fatty parenchyma and is entirely submitted  SECTION CODE  I J  Medial margin L N  Inferior margin O P  Lateral margin Q S  Superior margin T Z  Mid portion Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  final anterior margin  is a 5 x 4 x 0 8cm fatty breast tissue fragment with a stitch on the black inked surface designating furthest from tumor  The opposite surface is inked blue and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fatty parenchyma and entirely submitted in AA KK  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  axillary contents   are two fragments of fatty tissue measuring 11 x 7 x 3cm in aggregate  Dissection of the specimen reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  The small lymph nodes are submitted entirely and REMOVED_DATE of a large lymph node is submitted in LL QQ  Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  FIRM AREA OF TUMOR WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF ANTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  Mari Mino  MD O R  Diagnosis by  William C  Faquin MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  PART C  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN  PART D  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  , Unchecked.
