breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 07 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number   Breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cauterized fibroadipose tissue with a localizing guide wire and an accompanying mammogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm firm  slightly gritty  irregular tan white region focally abutting the inked resection margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in A M  with the firm region in A D and other suspicious areas from microcalcifications in F I  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT MASS   EXCISION  SUSPICIOUS AREA IS TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
