Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 19 22 CLINICAL DATA  Bowtie is new inferior margin  Long stitch lateral  short stitch anterior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 3  MULTIPLE MICROSCOPIC FOCI PRESENT IN 4 OF 10 TISSUE BLOCKS  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR  ANTERIOR AND INFERIOR MARGINS IN SEVERAL FOCI  SEE NOTE   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA   0 05CM   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Immunostains for p63  calponin and heavy chain myosin support the in situ nature of the neoplastic process  A single focus   0 05cm  on slide B is suspicious but not diagnostic for microinvasion  this focus is not present on the immunohistochemical stained levels of this slide  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17 04                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  short anterior  lateral  bowtie new inferior margin left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm portion of tan pink fibroadipose tissue with a bowtie stitch designating the inferior  a long black stitch the lateral  the short black stitch the anterior margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the inferior green and the superior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm cavity which communicates with the supero anterior  superior  and superior posterior margins  Surrounding the cavity is a diffuse yellow orange area consistent with fat necrosis that focally abuts the margin  The remaining cut surface shows diffuse cystic change and dense grey white fibrous tissue with no discrete nodules or other gross abnormalities  A silver metal clip is located within the fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as A J  The tissue adjacent to the silver metal clip is submitted in H  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
