s a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue with a stitch at one edge  One of two flat aspects of the specimen is fibrotic and granular  This aspect is regarded as the resection margin  The surgeon was contacted and after discussion with her  the opposite aspect is inked black as the new true margin  The granular aspect is left un inked and the specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right final margin superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with a fibrous and granular surface on one flat aspect and an unremarkable soft adipose surface on the other  A stitch is present on one of the ends of the specimen between the two sides  Per the surgeon  the non granular side is considered the probable new  true  margin and is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final margin inferior   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with a concave  granular  fibrous area on one aspect and unremarkable fibrofatty tissue on the other flat aspect  There is a black stitch through one thin edge of the specimen  Per the surgeon  the non granular side is considered the probable new  true  margin and is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right breast final margin medial   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with two flat aspects  one of which is somewhat concave and granular with the other unremarkable  There is a black stitch in one edge of the specimen  Per the surgeon  this side is taken as the probable new  true  margin and is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M